WEBVTT

00:09.480 --> 00:14.910
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold
in Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

01:30.660 --> 01:34.000
Miss Adelaide's debut!

01:38.250 --> 01:39.700
Oh!

01:46.180 --> 01:48.370
Do you think you can catch me?

01:50.390 --> 01:52.660
What beauty and charm!

01:53.330 --> 01:54.800
She really is like a fairy!

01:55.210 --> 01:57.510
<i>Modern technology's really helping me out!</i>

02:02.300 --> 02:03.960
I will not retreat!

02:05.920 --> 02:06.980
Face my wrath!

02:29.330 --> 02:32.330
Beatrice the Charmer

02:33.130 --> 02:36.040
<i>Adelaide's debutante ball 
went off without a hitch!</i>

02:36.040 --> 02:38.300
<i>General Store Mitsuha's open 
for business again!</i>

02:38.300 --> 02:41.590
<b>Enjoy Softer Skin
Moisturizing Soap</b>

02:38.300 --> 02:41.590
<b>Small Gift</b>

02:38.300 --> 02:41.590
<b>General Store
Mitsuha</b>

02:38.710 --> 02:41.590
Oh! Are you okay giving away 
something so luxurious?

02:41.590 --> 02:44.530
Thank you for always being so kind to me.

02:44.530 --> 02:47.110
I'm glad you seem to be doing well.

02:47.110 --> 02:49.510
The shop's been closed 
for a while, hasn't it?

02:49.510 --> 02:52.170
I was worried something might have happened.

02:52.170 --> 02:55.640
I'm so sorry for making you worry.

02:56.400 --> 02:58.950
<i>Japanese city folk have 
never treated me so kindly!</i>

02:58.950 --> 03:01.240
<i>Ah, how heartwarming!</i>

03:03.220 --> 03:06.000
Thank you for your purchase!

03:06.000 --> 03:09.190
<i>Looking good, with a steady rise 
in both customers and sales!</i>

03:09.190 --> 03:10.320
<i>All right!</i>

03:10.320 --> 03:14.140
I earned 260 gold from 
Adelaide's debutante ball...

03:14.140 --> 03:18.190
The equivalent of 26,000,000 yen 
in this world's monetary value!

03:18.190 --> 03:19.880
That's a hefty profit!

03:20.930 --> 03:23.020
I made sure to take photos 
and recordings, as well!

03:23.020 --> 03:27.520
I'll print a number of stills and sell them 
off to the viscount at a steep price!

03:27.520 --> 03:31.390
Echigoya, you are a wicked one indeed.

03:31.390 --> 03:35.140
I daresay not as wicked as you, magistrate!

03:35.850 --> 03:37.010
Ah, yes!

03:37.010 --> 03:38.860
Welcome...

03:38.860 --> 03:40.500
Give me some fish.

03:40.500 --> 03:41.150
Pardon?

03:41.150 --> 03:43.780
Hurry up and give me some fish!

03:46.100 --> 03:48.980
Um, this is actually a general store.

03:48.980 --> 03:52.120
If you want some fish, you'd have 
better luck at the fishmonger—

03:52.120 --> 03:53.270
Enough with the charade!

03:53.270 --> 03:56.000
I'm already fully aware 
that you sell fish here!

03:56.000 --> 03:58.950
Make haste with the fish, or else 
you'll get what's coming to you!

03:58.950 --> 04:00.340
Huh? What would that be, exactly?

04:00.340 --> 04:01.620
How dare you?!

04:01.620 --> 04:04.680
Do you think you can escape 
the wrath of Baron Turk unscathed?!

04:04.680 --> 04:07.790
What? You're a baron?

04:08.640 --> 04:10.960
O-Of course not!

04:10.960 --> 04:13.020
I'm the head chef for Baron Turk's house!

04:13.390 --> 04:16.340
<i>I can tell from your attire 
that you're no aristocrat.</i>

04:16.340 --> 04:19.780
So what business does the head 
chef of a baron have with us?

04:20.320 --> 04:24.370
Lately, the master says 
my cooking's not good,

04:24.370 --> 04:27.230
and that he'd rather eat 
some other cuisine instead.

04:27.660 --> 04:32.250
Upon inquiry, he raved about 
the exotic fish he tried at a recent party,

04:32.250 --> 04:33.790
and how delicious it was!

04:33.790 --> 04:36.830
<i>Oh! The food really had a resounding effect!</i>

04:38.140 --> 04:42.980
With good ingredients, I could 
make dishes that are just as good!

04:42.980 --> 04:45.000
If only I had the ingredients!

04:45.000 --> 04:49.640
Well... we didn't actually 
sell them the fish.

04:50.000 --> 04:52.590
In the process of coordinating 
the entire party as per agreement,

04:52.590 --> 04:56.500
we supplied it as a necessary component 
in fulfilling our contractual obligation.

04:56.500 --> 04:59.400
That is to say, we're not 
in the business of selling fish.

04:59.400 --> 05:02.970
You're trying to trick me by 
spouting your nonsense excuses!

05:02.970 --> 05:05.390
If you don't shut up and do as I say...

05:06.660 --> 05:08.320
Quite the commotion, I see.

05:10.320 --> 05:12.350
Just what is going on here?

05:13.860 --> 05:15.840
<i>Oh! Lady Iris makes her grand entrance!</i>

05:15.840 --> 05:17.130
A-A noblewoman?!

05:19.860 --> 05:22.170
Mitsuha! Why haven't you visited?!

05:22.170 --> 05:25.100
<i>Shoot, it completely slipped my mind.</i>

05:25.100 --> 05:29.600
Ah, well, er... I've just been so busy...

05:29.600 --> 05:31.230
With this fellow?

05:31.230 --> 05:34.080
Who is he? A customer of yours?

05:34.080 --> 05:37.140
No, he's not a customer. Not at all.

05:37.480 --> 05:38.460
You see...

05:38.460 --> 05:42.580
He said he'd hurt me 
if I didn't do as he says,

05:42.580 --> 05:45.570
so I was just at a loss 
as to what I should do...

05:44.760 --> 05:45.570
What?!

05:46.330 --> 05:48.530
What... are you saying?!

05:49.020 --> 05:51.990
What business do you have with my daughter?

05:53.570 --> 05:55.530
No, I'm just a customer...

05:55.530 --> 05:57.740
He said he's with Baron Turk's house.

05:57.740 --> 06:00.560
Saying he'd hurt me 
if I didn't do as he says...

06:00.560 --> 06:02.130
I'm terribly sorry!

06:03.400 --> 06:05.970
I'll lodge a complaint 
with the baron afterwards.

06:05.970 --> 06:09.550
Thank you so much, Count! Lady Iris!

06:10.730 --> 06:11.730
Eh?

06:12.510 --> 06:14.650
Let us be off, then, Mitsuha.

06:14.650 --> 06:17.020
Oh, no!

06:17.790 --> 06:22.060
<i>General Store Mitsuha 
was forced to close for the day.</i>

06:39.050 --> 06:43.040
<i>And that's how Colette discovered 
the law of universal gravitation...</i>

06:43.440 --> 06:44.710
<i>As if!</i>

06:48.610 --> 06:49.880
Mitsuha!

06:49.880 --> 06:52.260
Oh, it's Mitsuha!

06:53.040 --> 06:53.890
<i>Huh?</i>

06:53.890 --> 06:56.310
<i>Is it me or is she acting 
a little overly familiar?</i>

06:56.310 --> 07:00.420
<i>Well, that's just a sign of her affection.</i>

07:00.420 --> 07:01.230
<i>Okay!</i>

07:02.370 --> 07:04.190
Long time no see, Beatrice!

07:04.610 --> 07:07.540
Mitsuha, what have you 
been up to all this time?

07:07.540 --> 07:10.520
Mitsuha organized the 
debutante ball for Miss Adelaide,

07:10.520 --> 07:13.230
Viscount Reiner's daughter.

07:14.660 --> 07:18.870
The dishes and sweets from Mitsuha's country
were all like nothing I'd seen before,

07:18.870 --> 07:20.660
but they were all so delicious!

07:21.060 --> 07:24.860
The short performance written by Mitsuha 
was quite entertaining, as well.

07:24.860 --> 07:26.090
How could you be so cruel?!

07:26.090 --> 07:30.100
Why was I the only one 
not invited to such a fun party?!

07:30.990 --> 07:33.690
You know you're not a debutante yet...

07:33.690 --> 07:35.350
You'll have to wait another two years.

07:37.310 --> 07:38.770
Delicious food!

07:38.770 --> 07:39.780
Sweets!

07:39.780 --> 07:41.310
Entertaining performances!

07:41.310 --> 07:44.270
Delicious food! Sweets!

07:44.270 --> 07:45.980
I forgot! I must be off!

07:46.580 --> 07:47.650
<i>They ran away...</i>

07:47.650 --> 07:49.090
Hey, Mitsuha...

07:49.440 --> 07:51.970
What about my debutante ball?

07:51.970 --> 07:54.070
Will you take charge and organize it?!

07:54.070 --> 07:55.960
O-Of course!

07:55.960 --> 07:58.640
If that's what you want, I'd love to!

07:58.640 --> 07:59.650
Really?

08:00.130 --> 08:01.420
Really!

08:02.180 --> 08:03.790
Really and truly?

08:03.790 --> 08:05.750
Really and truly!

08:07.010 --> 08:09.070
It's a promise, Mitsuha!

08:10.910 --> 08:13.860
<i>Phew, looks like I'm safe for now...</i>

08:13.860 --> 08:16.640
Well then, let us have dinner first.

08:17.510 --> 08:20.580
We can have a nice, long chat afterwards.

08:20.580 --> 08:21.850
Miss Mitsuha.

08:32.910 --> 08:38.050
I'd never have imagined you would 
direct Miss Adelaide's debutante ball.

08:38.050 --> 08:42.260
I was really taken by surprise 
when I spotted you there.

08:42.260 --> 08:46.560
I was so busy, I didn't get a chance 
to get in touch with you all.

08:46.560 --> 08:47.960
I'm so sorry.

08:48.490 --> 08:51.330
No, it's nothing to apologize for.

08:51.330 --> 08:55.220
I must say though, the way you organized 
that party was just spectacular.

08:56.060 --> 08:58.710
It's an honor to hear that from you.

08:58.710 --> 09:00.560
Thank you very much!

09:00.560 --> 09:03.530
So, where did that cuisine come from?

09:03.530 --> 09:04.690
Those moving pictures, as well.

09:04.690 --> 09:08.520
And how did you get those peculiar 
articles you sell in the shop?

09:08.520 --> 09:11.040
Ah, well...

09:11.040 --> 09:13.110
<i>Figures!</i>

09:13.110 --> 09:17.080
<i>All right then, what's my excuse this time?</i>

09:23.150 --> 09:23.980
<i>Ah!</i>

09:24.440 --> 09:25.560
All of those...

09:25.560 --> 09:28.440
are from my friends back home,

09:28.440 --> 09:30.920
worried I was down on my luck 
in a foreign country,

09:30.920 --> 09:34.350
who sent me all those items 
behind the authorities' back.

09:34.350 --> 09:37.230
I see, your friends back home.

09:37.230 --> 09:38.140
Yes.

09:38.560 --> 09:41.540
I went through all the food at the party,

09:41.540 --> 09:45.350
but they sent me too many everyday items, 
so I'm selling what's left over.

09:45.350 --> 09:48.910
All of that? How did they bring all of it?

09:48.910 --> 09:54.050
It seems my friends dispatched small, 
high-speed ferries, one after another,

09:54.050 --> 09:57.440
and they secretly dock at night 
to transport everything.

09:57.440 --> 09:59.220
I'm struggling here!

09:59.220 --> 10:01.530
I hope I'm not contradicting 
what I said earlier.

10:05.270 --> 10:08.330
<i>Well... I'm feigning a little bit here.</i>

10:08.330 --> 10:11.340
<i>I'm hoping they can be so kind 
as to ignore any inconsistencies!</i>

10:13.850 --> 10:15.760
Well, no need to worry 
ourselves with details.

10:16.160 --> 10:18.020
We all know how Mitsuha is.

10:18.020 --> 10:20.460
You're right. It <i>is</i> Mitsuha.

10:20.460 --> 10:22.220
Wait, what do you mean by that?!

10:22.220 --> 10:25.200
What? Would you prefer we dig deeper?

10:25.200 --> 10:27.880
No, it's nothing. I'm sorry.

10:29.440 --> 10:32.340
No, this is no trifling matter.

10:32.340 --> 10:36.230
Mitsuha, your enigmatic nature 
enhances your beauty.

10:36.740 --> 10:40.860
More so than Miss Adelaide, 
the debutante taking center stage,

10:41.460 --> 10:44.440
Mitsuha, you were the one 
I found enchanting that night.

10:44.440 --> 10:45.760
My lady.

10:45.760 --> 10:50.920
<i>Back then, you were aggressively 
making a move on Adelaide...</i>

10:51.290 --> 10:54.900
<i>Oh... what an icy glare, Mitsuha!</i>

10:54.900 --> 10:56.880
<i>But that's what I love about you!</i>

10:56.880 --> 10:59.840
<i>This guy's got a screw loose...</i>

11:01.090 --> 11:03.600
Leaving that aside, Mitsuha...

11:03.600 --> 11:08.060
Er... it's getting quite late, 
so I should get going...

11:08.060 --> 11:09.720
The night is still young.

11:09.720 --> 11:12.080
I have much to ask you,

11:12.080 --> 11:14.560
in regards to man-made humanoid 
golems, for example.

11:14.560 --> 11:15.520
Huh?

11:15.520 --> 11:17.220
What the heck are those?!

11:17.220 --> 11:21.610
Don't you remember our rousing discussion 
when you stayed the night at the manor?

11:21.610 --> 11:23.710
What?! Did we really discuss that?

11:23.710 --> 11:25.990
I'm sorry, I don't remember that at all.

11:25.990 --> 11:27.610
I-I see.

11:27.610 --> 11:29.670
What about our talk of salt production?

11:29.670 --> 11:31.880
That I remember all too clearly!

11:31.880 --> 11:33.710
Your territory overlooks the sea, right?

11:33.710 --> 11:35.320
In that case, for salt production,

11:35.320 --> 11:39.070
you can use banked, channeled, 
or sloping salt terraces!

11:39.070 --> 11:42.980
First, you need to consider your 
land's coastline and population...

11:40.060 --> 11:44.400
<i>As it turns out, I ended up staying 
the night at the count's manor.</i>

11:51.730 --> 11:53.640
Ah, I'm so tired!

11:54.380 --> 11:57.230
We ended up talking for so long!

11:58.010 --> 12:02.090
They really are so nice 
and fun to be with, though.

12:02.090 --> 12:04.200
Everyone in the count's family, that is.

12:06.480 --> 12:07.410
Yes?

12:13.030 --> 12:15.180
Beatrice?

12:16.960 --> 12:19.960
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

12:19.960 --> 12:22.970
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

12:28.740 --> 12:31.250
<i>What could it be so late at night?</i>

12:31.250 --> 12:34.410
<i>Are things not going well with her parents?</i>

12:34.410 --> 12:37.780
<i>I can't imagine that 
happening in this family...</i>

12:37.780 --> 12:39.260
<i>Relationship talk, then?!</i>

12:39.260 --> 12:40.670
<i>Or could it be...</i>

12:40.670 --> 12:44.630
<i>that she's in love with me, as well?!</i>

12:44.630 --> 12:45.860
Mitsuha?

12:46.590 --> 12:48.240
Y-Yeah, what is it?

12:48.670 --> 12:51.820
About what we talked about earlier...

12:51.820 --> 12:55.650
Huh? Earlier? What was it again?

12:55.650 --> 12:58.100
What? You don't remember?!

12:58.100 --> 13:01.320
You said you'd take care 
of my debutante ball, as well!

13:01.320 --> 13:03.830
O-Of course I remember that!

13:03.830 --> 13:05.690
I haven't forgotten!

13:07.720 --> 13:09.490
Really, truly, and surely?

13:09.490 --> 13:11.560
Really, truly, and surely!

13:11.560 --> 13:14.660
You'll make it an amazing, unbeatable event?

13:14.660 --> 13:17.610
N-Naturally! All for you, Beatrice!

13:17.610 --> 13:19.950
I'm so glad!

13:19.950 --> 13:21.400
So what'll it be like?

13:21.890 --> 13:24.860
Hmm, let me think...

13:24.860 --> 13:26.570
For example...

13:28.310 --> 13:32.210
At night, you'll ride in a carriage 
decked out with decorations...

13:32.210 --> 13:33.290
Yeah, yeah!

13:34.210 --> 13:36.820
And take part in an animal parade!

13:37.900 --> 13:39.340
Animals?

13:40.710 --> 13:40.960
<b>Buttered Potatoes</b>

13:40.710 --> 13:43.710
Corn Dogs

13:40.710 --> 13:43.710
Shaved Ice

13:40.710 --> 13:46.760
<b>Buttered Potat</b>

13:40.710 --> 13:48.930
Takoyaki

13:40.710 --> 13:48.930
Delicious

13:40.710 --> 13:48.930
<b>Buttered Potatoes</b>

13:41.300 --> 13:43.550
We'll serve food from exotic food stalls.

13:43.550 --> 13:44.660
How about takoya—

13:44.660 --> 13:46.570
Grilled octopus in wheat flour...

13:46.570 --> 13:48.930
and cotton-like candy confections?

13:49.370 --> 13:52.010
Octopus? Cotton?

13:52.010 --> 13:53.640
Sounds hard to eat...

13:54.020 --> 13:57.330
And we can shoot off a whole 
bunch of real pretty fireworks!

13:57.330 --> 13:59.570
Fireworks? What are those?

13:59.570 --> 14:01.200
Ah, you see...

14:01.200 --> 14:05.740
You launch fireballs to fill the sky 
with flower-like patterns.

14:05.740 --> 14:08.070
It's magic native to my country.

14:08.620 --> 14:10.530
That sounds amazing!

14:11.770 --> 14:13.890
Is that really possible?!

14:15.280 --> 14:17.830
Mitsuha! Promise me!

14:17.830 --> 14:19.500
You absolutely must have those!

14:19.990 --> 14:22.090
Y...Yeah.

14:22.620 --> 14:25.210
<i>Here's hoping she forgets 
in the next two years!</i>

14:26.850 --> 14:29.080
That's one less thing to worry about!

14:30.580 --> 14:32.720
I realized it when I worked with Adelaide,

14:32.720 --> 14:35.780
but a debutante ball sure 
is a big deal, huh?

14:35.780 --> 14:37.420
Well, of course it is!

14:37.420 --> 14:41.940
For us daughters of noblemen, 
it's the biggest event of our lives!

14:41.940 --> 14:45.940
In your life... 
But it's only at the age of 15!

14:45.940 --> 14:47.980
What are you saying, Mitsuha?

14:47.980 --> 14:50.660
Girls get engaged when they're 10 years old,

14:50.660 --> 14:53.020
and become adults and get married at 15!

14:53.020 --> 14:54.160
It's only natural!

14:54.160 --> 14:55.270
Eh?

14:55.270 --> 14:58.030
So does that mean you're already...

14:58.030 --> 15:02.390
Nope, still no engagement offers for me.

15:02.390 --> 15:05.130
But you're fighting for your life at 13!

15:05.660 --> 15:06.930
That reminds me!

15:06.930 --> 15:10.440
I have a friend, Sestalia, 
who has a lovely fiancé,

15:10.440 --> 15:12.760
and yet she's sleeping 
with Eilish, as well...

15:12.760 --> 15:14.940
Also, also...

15:13.020 --> 15:16.910
<i>Do aristocratic girls all mature this early?!</i>

15:16.910 --> 15:18.460
<i>Say it ain't so!</i>

15:18.460 --> 15:20.460
So what about you, Mitsuha?

15:20.460 --> 15:21.240
Eh?

15:21.240 --> 15:23.580
Dating boys, I mean.

15:24.710 --> 15:26.190
Well...

15:26.190 --> 15:30.750
I-I was popular with 
the boys back in my country, too!

15:26.190 --> 15:30.950
<b>I Shall Survive
Using Potions!</b>

15:30.750 --> 15:35.090
I knew a lot about their hobbies, 
so they invited me to play,

15:35.090 --> 15:37.160
and asked me to tell them 
interesting stories.

15:37.160 --> 15:41.730
Well, I wasn't very athletic, 
so when they needed to fill teams...

15:41.730 --> 15:44.380
Or that... and you know...

15:44.890 --> 15:46.840
That doesn't count as being popular!

15:47.370 --> 15:48.630
<i>I figured as much!</i>

15:48.630 --> 15:51.450
<i>F-For now, let's change the topic.</i>

15:51.450 --> 15:53.250
A-Anyway, about your—

15:53.250 --> 15:56.090
Well? That's not what I meant!

15:56.090 --> 15:59.060
You've never actually dated a boy?

15:59.060 --> 16:01.610
<i>Sh-She won't let me change the topic!</i>

16:03.240 --> 16:05.240
Well? How about it, Mitsuha?

16:05.240 --> 16:08.230
I won't tell anyone, so be honest with me.

16:09.530 --> 16:12.200
G-Guess I haven't.

16:12.200 --> 16:15.700
So what would be your type 
if you were going to date someone?

16:17.750 --> 16:20.240
My ideal type, huh?

16:20.240 --> 16:23.160
<i>That's surprisingly hard to pin down...</i>

16:23.160 --> 16:24.960
Anything's fine!

16:24.960 --> 16:28.780
His looks, his personality, 
his social status...

16:28.780 --> 16:32.030
Er... Or his fortune?

16:32.030 --> 16:33.480
Hold it right there!

16:33.480 --> 16:36.360
Beatrice, what was that just now?

16:36.360 --> 16:39.350
Huh? I-I'm not looking at anything! I swear!

16:39.790 --> 16:42.060
That's a lie!

16:42.060 --> 16:45.310
Who was it that asked you?

16:50.790 --> 16:53.750
So? What's going on?

16:53.750 --> 16:55.260
Well...

16:57.230 --> 17:00.720
I guess we can forget about 
that debutante ball, then.

17:00.720 --> 17:02.060
I-I'm sorry!

17:02.060 --> 17:04.220
I'll tell you! I'll tell you!

17:05.440 --> 17:08.460
That was from Brother Alex...

17:08.460 --> 17:10.100
Mm-hmm.

17:10.100 --> 17:12.750
And this is from Brother Theo...

17:12.750 --> 17:14.170
Him, too?

17:14.640 --> 17:17.890
And this one... is from Father.

17:17.890 --> 17:18.680
What?!

17:19.070 --> 17:20.620
<i>The count, as well?</i>

17:20.620 --> 17:24.070
The three of them said if I could 
find out the answer to these questions,

17:24.070 --> 17:26.140
they'd pay me one gold.

17:26.140 --> 17:27.400
I see now...

17:27.400 --> 17:30.120
Mitsuha, that's why...

17:30.120 --> 17:31.510
I understand.

17:31.510 --> 17:33.660
Then one gold for me, as well.

17:33.660 --> 17:34.400
Eh?

17:34.820 --> 17:37.610
You've got your reputation, as well, right?

17:37.610 --> 17:40.430
So one gold as my fee.

17:40.900 --> 17:42.370
I'll cooperate for that.

17:42.370 --> 17:43.600
Mitsuha!

17:43.600 --> 17:47.810
However, don't say I answered 
your questions directly.

17:47.810 --> 17:50.290
Tell them you worked 
those answers out of me.

17:50.290 --> 17:52.750
Okay, got it!

17:52.750 --> 17:57.120
<i>I can use this to mislead 
the count and the boys.</i>

17:57.120 --> 18:01.260
<i>You don't stand a chance in hell 
against me in an information war!</i>

18:01.770 --> 18:03.390
To be completely honest,

18:03.390 --> 18:07.860
I tried so hard to come up with ways 
to get some real answers out of you.

18:07.860 --> 18:09.150
So thank goodness.

18:09.150 --> 18:10.580
Thanks, Mitsuha!

18:10.580 --> 18:11.890
Huh? Wait.

18:11.890 --> 18:14.100
So since the moment I opened the door,

18:14.100 --> 18:20.060
you were putting on an act the whole time 
to get information from me?

18:20.060 --> 18:22.390
Yes... well...

18:23.540 --> 18:25.120
<i>Beatrice...</i>

18:25.680 --> 18:28.240
<i>What a terrifying girl, breasts and all!</i>

18:35.930 --> 18:37.420
<i>The next day...</i>

18:37.820 --> 18:40.900
With this weather, 
I can't expect any customers...

18:42.050 --> 18:46.310
The people in this world stay inside 
when it looks like rain.

18:46.910 --> 18:49.930
I haven't seen a single person 
use an umbrella...

18:51.070 --> 18:53.340
What if I sell umbrellas, then?!

18:54.310 --> 18:55.280
Welcome...

18:59.580 --> 19:02.340
<i>He's clearly not your average customer.</i>

19:02.340 --> 19:03.980
<i>Is he on the run from someone?</i>

19:05.300 --> 19:06.740
<i>Firearm, check!</i>

19:06.740 --> 19:08.590
<i>Knife, check!</i>

19:11.830 --> 19:14.040
<i>That outfit... could it be?!</i>

19:15.880 --> 19:18.990
I know you've taken refuge in this shop.

19:18.990 --> 19:20.840
Iaps, killer of your master!

19:21.160 --> 19:21.930
Quiet!

19:24.140 --> 19:26.670
You've got a bounty on your head.

19:26.670 --> 19:28.350
Come quietly with me!

19:28.350 --> 19:30.820
I won't be taken in so easily!

19:30.820 --> 19:32.560
I'm taking this brat hostage!

19:33.250 --> 19:34.650
Who're you calling a brat?!

19:35.040 --> 19:35.980
Balse!

19:38.590 --> 19:40.580
My eyes! My eyes!

19:43.950 --> 19:46.160
Hey, give me my knife back!

19:46.880 --> 19:50.370
<i>No one gets away 
with stealing </i>my<i> merchandise!</i>

19:54.430 --> 19:56.270
Stop!

19:56.270 --> 19:57.090
Eh?

19:57.710 --> 19:58.630
It's dangerous.

19:58.630 --> 20:00.810
But he's going to get away!

20:00.810 --> 20:01.720
No need to worry.

20:06.570 --> 20:09.080
You're not getting past this point.

20:17.930 --> 20:19.650
There's nowhere left to run.

20:19.650 --> 20:20.610
Not yet!

20:22.630 --> 20:24.320
And now a swordsman!

20:24.320 --> 20:27.030
But at this distance, 
a knife is the faster weapon!

20:27.920 --> 20:30.790
I see no need to draw my sword against you.

20:31.150 --> 20:33.830
D-Don't mess with me!

20:38.590 --> 20:40.210
Whoa!

20:42.130 --> 20:44.670
The conditions are we take you alive.

20:44.670 --> 20:46.300
You're coming quietly with us.

20:46.300 --> 20:49.240
G-Goddamn it!

20:55.340 --> 20:57.860
<i>These four are the ones 
I've been waiting for!</i>

20:58.480 --> 21:01.070
<i>A beautiful, gallant swordswoman!</i>

21:01.510 --> 21:03.780
<i>A baby-faced spearman!</i>

21:04.360 --> 21:06.910
<i>A veteran warrior wielding a greatsword!</i>

21:06.910 --> 21:08.680
<i>An archer girl!</i>

21:08.680 --> 21:10.120
<i>That can only mean...</i>

21:10.120 --> 21:13.460
Finally! Now this is a fantasy staple!

21:13.460 --> 21:15.330
The very image of adventurers!

21:15.960 --> 21:18.830
Adventurers? What are you talking about?

21:18.830 --> 21:22.300
We're mercenaries who take 
on jobs from our guild.

21:22.300 --> 21:24.400
A mercenary guild!

21:24.400 --> 21:26.800
Also an RPG classic!

21:29.020 --> 21:32.310
If you're in a guild, does that mean 
you take on missions from anyone?

21:32.620 --> 21:34.170
Y-Yeah...

21:34.170 --> 21:37.750
As long as it abides by the law 
and guild regulations, at least.

21:37.750 --> 21:40.780
Of course, it doesn't come cheap...

21:40.780 --> 21:44.280
And can I also ask for specific mercenaries?

21:44.280 --> 21:45.830
That goes without saying.

21:45.830 --> 21:50.300
Then can you take on a mission for me?

21:50.300 --> 21:51.080
Eh?

21:51.640 --> 21:53.950
Eh?!
